Hmm, but synchronizing on getProps() only protects if writes also synchronize on the same object. Properties extends Hashtable, which is synchronized on itself, but iteration over entrySet is not atomic. Since Properties is a Hashtable, iterating entrySet while another thread does setProperty throws CME. Synchronizing on the properties object while iterating, plus setters going through Properties.setProperty (which synchronizes on the Properties object itself as a Hashtable method), makes it consistent! Because Hashtable methods synchronize on `this` — so `synchronized(properties)` blocks any concurrent `setProperty`. That's the actual upstream fix.

